# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Recorded media and derived tensors NEVER enter git.
#
# A repo that has once held large binaries stays bloated permanently: the blobs
# live in history even after deletion, and every future clone pays for them.
# Recorded media is backed up separately (external drive + offsite copy).
#
# What IS versioned: code, configs, and the small text files whose history is
# the point -- manifest.csv, signers.csv, and the gloss prompt list. Those are
# whitelisted with ! rules below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw video, in any location
*.mp4
*.mov
*.avi
*.mkv
*.webm

# Cached landmark tensors
*.npy
*.npz

# Data directories (recorded takes, extracted landmarks, archival copies)
data/
!msl/data/
raw/
archive/
landmark_cache/

# Re-admit the dataset record itself: small, text, and its history matters.
!**/manifest.csv
!**/signers.csv
!**/prompts/**/*.txt
!**/prompts/**/*.csv

# Model artifacts
*.pt
*.pth
*.ckpt
*.onnx
checkpoints/
runs/
outputs/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
